# Code Quality

## Language & style

- Frontend: TypeScript, functional components + hooks. Avoid `any`; type API payloads and props.
- Backend: CommonJS JavaScript matching existing controllers/models.
- Prefer clear names over clever abstractions; keep diffs focused on the task.

## Errors & async

```ts
// ❌ BAD
try { await api.get('/x'); } catch (e) {}

// ✅ GOOD
try {
  await api.get('/x');
} catch (error: unknown) {
  const message =
    (error as { response?: { data?: { message?: string } } })?.response?.data?.message
    || t('msg.somethingWentWrong');
  showToast(message, 'error');
}
```

- Never swallow errors. Always handle loading → success/empty → error in UI that fetches.
- Guard `useEffect` fetches with `user?.id` / active tab; cancel or ignore stale responses when tab changes.

## Lists & state

- Client lists: `useListPagination` + `ListPagination` (default page size 10).
- Controlled forms; don’t leave orphaned state when closing `SlideOver` / modals.
- Map status enums to labels via existing helpers — never show raw DB enums in UI.

## i18n

- All user-visible strings via `t('key')` — no hardcoded English/Swedish in JSX.
- Add keys to **both** `locales/en.json` and `locales/sv.json`.

## Reuse before invent

- Buttons: `.btn-save`, `.btn-approve`, `.btn-reject`, `.btn-cancel`, `.btn-delete`, `.btn-close`.
- Inputs: `.input-brand`; dates: `DateOnlyPicker`; icons: `lucide-react` only.
- Toasts: `useToast().showToast(message, 'success' | 'error' | 'warning' | 'info')`.

## Glitch prevention checklist

- [ ] Empty `catch` or missing toast on failed mutation?
- [ ] Missing loading/empty state on lists?
- [ ] Effect missing dependency causing double-fetch or stale tab data?
- [ ] Untranslated string or only one locale updated?
- [ ] New one-off color/button instead of existing class?
